# doubt — the player may say NO to what a thinking proposes, and the thinking tries again
#
# A pineal gland of 3 gives three retries and the doubt (DoubtStat, at 2 or more). While a retry
# remains, the reasoning ends on a question and the preview box asks YES or NO before the action modus
# mentis is asked. Here the first answer is NO: the mind voices its doubt holding, crosses the pair off
# and reasons again (at seed 42 the same goal, climbing back down, by another means) — and the second
# answer is YES (advance answers YES when no `doubt` is queued),
# which the mind voices too before the action is written. One thinking, one button.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Crown" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Giant Tree" --grant-mm woodcraft --organs pineal_gland=3

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
advance 12 180

doubt no
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
# Expected text is matched line by line on the wrapped screen, hence the short fragments.
expect But is it truly wise to
expect and it holds
expect another way
expect does not hold
expect I am resolved to
quit
